<title>MALAYSIA: Malaysia May 1-15 palm oil exports 264,659t - SGS.</title>
<headline>Malaysia May 1-15 palm oil exports 264,659t - SGS.</headline>
<dateline>KUALA LUMPUR 1997-05-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cargo surveyor Societe Generale de Surveillance (SGS) Malaysia Sdn Bhd said it estimated Malaysia's palm oil exports for May 1-15 at 264,659 tonnes against 336,791 tonnes for April 1-15.</p>
<p>It said the exports comprised 75,586 tonnes of RBD palm oil, 127,154 tonnes of RBD palm olein and 16,479 tonnes of RBD palm stearin. The other products totalled 45,440 tonnes.  </p>
<p>India was the top buyer during the period, taking 69,820 tonnes, followed by Pakistan which bought 56,750 tonnes, China (32,600 tonnes) and Japan (18,600 tonnes).</p>
<p>Countries in the European Union bought 14,844 tonnes.</p>
<p>-- Kuala Lumpur newsroom (603-230-7510)</p>
</text>
